{"code": "M11L2V6Q2", "page": 12, "stem_ok": false, "stem_book": "If the number of solutions of the equation cosθ − √3 sinθ = 1 in the interval [0, 2π] is K, then K²/2 is", "figure": null, "type": "numerical", "options_printed": false, "key": "4.5", "derived": "4.5", "verdict": "ok", "correct_answer": "4.5", "integer": false, "in_scope": true, "reason": "", "work": "2cos(θ + π/3) = 1 ⇒ θ = 2nπ or 2nπ − 2π/3 ⇒ θ = 0, 4π/3, 2π ⇒ K = 3 ⇒ K²/2 = 4.5"}
